														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4830022">
									

<p>Low-quality content naturally piles up in places like 682's termination log, 1459's extended logs, and other very large collaborative lists. Inevitably, a page curator has to go through and prune away the bad entries. I imagine that this is tiresome and time-consuming for the curator, and it also means that garbage entries in these logs live much longer than an equally garbage SCP would. If there were some way to install individual rating modules for each item on the log, so they could be voted on individually, then perhaps that might save some time for the curator and shorten the lifespan of the bad entries.</p>
<p>I thought that the log of extranormal events or unexplained locations was already like this, but it seems that I was mistaken.</p>

							</div>

								
					
