<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Comedy</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> This is an SCP based upon the narrative created by the song, Love Potion No. 9, made popular by The Clovers in 1959. The premise is that the SCP is the actual love potion described in the song, more or less. The object itself is a safe object, characterized as being an opaque black liquid contained within a small glass bottle. The liquid itself is described as smelling of turpentine. Its anomalous property is that it causes the drinker to lose all romantic and sexual discretion, except for a marked increase in the attractiveness of members of law enforcement.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> This object came to the attention of the Foundation after a young man was arrested and brought to a mental asylum after falling under the effects of the love potion and succeeding in his attempt to passionately kiss a police officer on patrol. The young man informed officials that he was compelled to behave in that manner after drinking a potion, created by a gypsy fortune teller named Madame Ruth in order to cure him of his bad luck with women.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> This is an SCP based on a well known piece of pop culture history. I feel like people will find it quite amusing and maybe even humorous.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I hope you guys see this as a lighthearted, humorous attempt at an SCP article.</p>

